From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryubing Android <ryubing-android@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] nce: offset the 39-bit kernel layout by the identity window base; fill GetInfo entropy

With an identity-mapped address space the kernel must lay the process out
inside the reserved host window (Eden passes fastmem_base as aslr_space_start).

- IProcessContext/ArmProcessContext/ProcessContext: expose AddressSpaceBase.
- KPageTable/KPageTableBase: accept the reserved base. For 39-bit processes with
  a base, code starts at base + 0x8000000 and AslrRegion = [base + 0x8000000,
  window end). The address space itself stays [0, 2^39) exactly like real
  hardware and Eden (m_address_space_start/end): rtld discovers the loaded NSOs
  by walking QueryMemory from address 0 until the cursor wraps, so an address
  space starting at the window base makes QueryMemory(0) return the "outside"
  descriptor (end wraps to 0), the walk ends before the first module and rtld
  aborts with "Unresolved symbol: nn::init::Start". Only region *placement*
  (alias/heap/stack/tlsio) is bounded to the window; they keep their real sizes
  when the window is >= 256 GiB and shrink for a 2^37 window (alias extra =
  window/8 in that case). Emits an NCE|LAYOUT line incl. the window.
- MemoryManagerHostNoMirror.IsRangeMapped (0011) returns false instead of
  throwing for VAs inside the kernel space but outside the window.
- KProcess: pass Context.AddressSpaceBase to KPageTable; fill RandomEntropy
  (svcGetInfo RandomEntropy was a TODO; nnSdk ASLR aborts on zero entropy).

